  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1226 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nOn Wednesday, a surface high will settle in for the day, resulting \nin comfortable afternoon temperatures along with primarily sunny \nskies. Return flow begins as early as Thursday morning despite mid-\nlevel zonal flow through late week. Medium range guidance differs on \nthe evolution of our next storm system. While the GFS brings a few \nshowers through on Thursday with the passage of a weak front and \nshortwave over north Texas, the ECMWF keeps this shortwave further \nnorth, resulting in dry weather Thursday and Friday.\n\nBy the weekend, another shot at rain may arrive in the form of an \nupper-level trough over northern Mexico. At this time, it is too \nearly to say how much of an impact this will have on our ambient \nweather. If this trough is too far south, most areas would likely \nremain dry Saturday, but if it is a bit further north as the ECMWF \nhas been advertising, then scattered showers are a better bet on \nSaturday. Much cooler temperatures are forecast for highs Saturday \nand Sunday as a front may bring an even cooler airmass into the \npicture, making it feel very Fall-like for the first full weekend of \nNovember.",
